hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19163","Surayj narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered announcement on the days of Tashriq that none enters Paradise but a believer, and they are days of eating and drinking."
"19164","Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Habib, from Nafi ibn Jubayr, from Bishr ibn Suhaym, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed on the days of Tashriq, then he mentioned like it, and said: These are days of eating and drinking."
"19165","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, and I heard it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shayba, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn al-Mughira al-Maafiri narrated to me, he said: Abd Allah ibn Bishr al-Khathami narrated to me, from his father, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Constantinople shall be opened; blessed the commander its commander and blessed the army that army. He said: So Maslama ibn Abd al-Malik called me and asked me, and I told him, so he raided Constantinople."
